\scanpage{494}
% 494-01: upper paragraph.
Even once the \unsure{ambiguity} of sign for
$\Theta_{\unsure{G}}^{\unsure{\pi}}$ is removed by passing to the two-sheeted extension
$\unsure{\widetilde{\mathcal T}_{1,1}}$ of
$\widetilde M_{0,3}$, the indeterminacy of the signs for
$\Theta_{\rho}^{\unsure{\pi}},\Theta_{\sigma}^{\unsure{\pi}}$
is not \unsure{removed} for all that, for the splittings
\deleted{$\unsure{\Psi_{\rho}^{\pi},\Psi_{\sigma}^{\pi}}$}
$\Psi_{1/2}^{\unsure{\pi}},\Psi_{-\overline{\mathrm j}}^{\unsure{\pi}}$)
are not for all that splittings (even partial!)
of \deleted{\unsure{this}} \unsure{the extension}
$\unsure{\widetilde{\mathcal T}_{1,1}}$, but only of
$\widetilde M_{0,3}$ --- and lifting them to splittings of
$\unsure{\widetilde{\mathcal T}_{1,1}}$
\inserted{over $\unsure{\mathcal T_{1,1}}$,}
amounts, very precisely, to choosing precisely elliptic curves with
Legendre rigidification over the points $1/2,-\overline{\mathrm j}$.
Thus, calculations made in terms of automorphisms of the groups with loops
$\widehat\Pi_{0,3}$ \unsure{or} \inserted{of}
$\unsure{\mathcal{C}}_{0,3}^{+\wedge}$,
\unsure{give back} \inserted{(without having \unsure{looked for} them!)}
results that fit very closely with particularly crucial
arithmetico-geometric truths.
\mspage{493}

